// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2429277257" "Aaron Walker is dead, but he may have been able to help the war effort with this one, single note of his."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4163386845" "{HeroName}, did you find Aaron Walker?<br><br>... I see. Aaron Walker was a good man, {HeroName}. I'm sure I don't need to tell you that. His death is but one of many caused by Cole's regime. Too many good men and women have died for Cole and his Praetors to build their empire. Let us make sure that Aaron is the last, and that his sacrifice will not be in vain.<br><br>You said he gave you a note? Hrm... Steven Sheridan! This is perfect, {HeroName}. I don't know how Aaron Walker found this out, but he may have just helped to save us all and move you forward."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Sheridan 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2625242687" "It's good to see another friendly face down here. I've heard about you through the grapevine. {HeroName}, wasn't it? I'm Dr. Steven Sheridan, here to help Longbow and the Resistance. If you've come down here through those monsters, you must have a good reason to see me."
// Answer Text :
"P2489748834" "(Explain the situation to Sheridan)"
// Page Page1 Text :
"P1408237563" "Hrmm... Interesting, very interesting. Can I see that data?<br><br><color orange>You hand the data over to Sheridan. He rubs his chin and takes out a small device.</color><br><br>I've run into issues like this in the past. It can be difficult to recover lost data, but I've created a device that can solve such problems. Just give it a moment for it to run..."
// Answer Text :
"P4043043368" "(Wait...)"
// Page Page2 Text :
"P2385686676" "<color orange>Dr. Sheridan's face pales as he watches his device.</color><br><br>{HeroName}... this is horrifying! The rest of the data! Look!"
// Answer Text :
"P865547946" "(Look at the data)"
// Page Choice1Page3 Text :
"P4168388306" "<color orange>Dr. Sheridan shows you the input on his device.</color><br><br>'Plans are ready to begin the war effort. Emperor Cole believes that the chaos on Primal Earth will spread into Praetoria soon. Already, we have seen Arachnos and Longbow causing terror in our streets. Primal Earth has entire armies of terrorists, monsters, and demons running about unchecked. If they were to find a way into Praetoria, we would all be doomed.<br><br>It is for that reason that we have worked tirelessly under the direction of Anti-Matter on these machines to bring the war to Primal Earth first. We will use the tower Neuron has built to create a portal big enough to fit the War Walkers. Once they are deployed, the war will be over within a week. Not even the Phalanx can withstand their might.<br><br>We have been ordered by Cole to take any non-super powered being prisoner and to have the Seers scan their minds to see if they are a threat. Any civilian who is not a threat will be allowed to live under Cole's new empire. We have also programmed the machines to avoid attacking civilians, though casualties due to collateral damage can not be avoided.<br><br>The main purpose is clear: we must destroy the threat on Primal Earth before it destroys us. Once that is done, we will wipe out the remainder of the Resistance. It is estimated we would only need one third of our machines to do so.'"
// Answer Text :
"P3618600331" ""A war with Primal Earth... and War Walkers?"
// Page Choice1Page4 Text :
"P3602393017" "It is as I feared.  We are too late to stop Cole from building an army. All we can do now is get everyone prepared for the worst.<br><br>I do not know when Cole plans to mobilize, but there <i>is</i> something we can do to slow him down. Take this drive. It will plant a virus inside of Neuron's tower, disabling its systems for some time. This will at least buy us and the Resistance some time.<br><br>I'm going to get to the nearest Resistance base to help them finish construction on a <color yellow>rift</color>. I don't have time to explain, but I believe you and I will meet again very soon. For now, you need to go and disable Neuron's tower!"
// Answer Text :
"P379498202" "Right, I'm on it!"
// Page Choice2Page3 Text :
"P324261669" "<color orange>You hear the sounds of the ghouls nearing the small group of Longbow.</color><br><br>Run, we will be fine!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P660737115" "I admit, I am somewhat surprised Steven Sheridan is here. It is perhaps the one intelligent thing I have witnessed Longbow do during my time here in Praetoria. Steven Sheridan is a brilliant scientist in Primal Earth and was once called <color yellow>Dr. Science.</color> He possesses possibly the most brilliant mind in the world. He may not have a mind that is as fast as our departed Aaron Walker, but he will be able to figure out what that data leads to if you bring it to him."
// SendOffString :
"P24342518" "Some of my own agents have told me that he is currently with a squad of Longbow deep in the tunnels beneath Neutropolis. We need to get Steven Sheridan onto the side of the Resistance and into safe hands as soon as possible.<br><br>I imagine he can prove a great help in bringing more aid through from Primal Earth, but if he were to be captured by Cole, then I fear all would be lost. Find Steven Sheridan and give him the data you have. He will be able to tell you what is happening and how exactly we can prevent it."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P125239213" "Meet with Steven Sheridan"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P355143090" "Steven Sheridan is our best hope to finding out what's in that data, {HeroName}."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P606016124" "<color deepskyblue>Part Three: Dr. Science to the Rescue</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P1886790660" "You can hear the faint sounds of the failed experiments in the tunnels. Somewhere here, Steven Sheridan awaits, holding the key to the fates of Primal Earth and Praetoria."

