// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2478826217" "You did well, {HeroName}. Sheridan is already with members of the Resistance and is quickly finishing up work that has been done on the <color yellow>Rift Enclosure</color>. It is a large gate that connects the world of Praetoria to the world of Primal Earth. It is through here that we in Primal Earth will send reinforcements to fight against Cole, though doing so will not be easy.<br><br>We can speak about that later, however. With Sheridan's virus, we have the advantage of surprise against Cole and Praetor Berry."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Marchand 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P1919792521" "Good to hear from you again, {HeroName}. What is your situation?"
// Answer Text :
"P2101500193" "(Explain everything you've discovered)"
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P998390989" "I see... so, you know of the plans for invasion. I have known this for quite some time, as you may imagine. It is a plan to protect the people of Praetoria, you must understand.<br><br>You've seen the influence that just <i>two</i> of the groups from that dimension have. They cause chaos and destruction, while we strive to create order and peace. The invasion is a way to ensure that this is maintained. It is that, or we fall into total chaos."
// Answer Text :
"P1852041237" "And what about killing all the supers in Primal Earth?"
// Page Noble Text :
"P880076058" "It... is not the first option that I wish for us, truth to be told. Starting a war will cost us many lives, even if we use the War Walkers. I have no doubt we will win, but it is an option that I would prefer to avoid. Unfortunately, this is not a view that many of the other Praetors share.<br><br>They are eager to wage war, knowing that <i>they</i> will not die in it. They do not realize the costs it will have on the normal people, both here and in Primal Earth. I have been doing my best to try to convince them to seek a peaceful solution, but my efforts have gone unheeded."
// Answer Text :
"P276917928" "So... what do you want me to do with this virus?"
// Page InformationPage2 Text :
"P2341087509" "<i>Plant it</i>. Plant it, and also enter in the code I'm sending to you. I want to track everything that Neuron is doing with that tower. If he sneezes, <i>I</i> want to know.<br><br>If we're going to go to war with Primal Earth, it's going to be because we have exhausted all other options. It will <i>not</i> be because of a group of Praetors who believe <i>they</i> are invincible."
// Answer Text :
"P855036618" "Alright, I'll do what I can, Marchand."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P399027902" "There's no time to lose, {HeroName}. I've analyzed the situation you're walking into. I believe Praetor Berry is becoming more suspicious that there may be a situation brewing around his tower. This does not mean that we should not take the fight to him. But you will have to be careful.<br><br>We will have to put the systems in Berry's tower on alert. According to Sheridan, this will leave a hole in its defenses for his virus. It would appear Berry is not a man who designs all of his technology... <i>perfectly</i>. To do this, you'll have to attack some of his Clockwork. This, in itself, should not be too hard, but I suspect Berry has put in place special defenses when this happens."
// AcceptString :
"P707658177" "Do you know what I should suspect?"
// SendOffString :
"P4149724691" "I have an idea.<br><br>I have still not found James Noble. Given that he went missing around the same time as Aaron Walker, I can only assume that Praetor Berry has retrieved his former experiment and put him to 'work', per say. This seems like it would be the exact opportunity he would use to test out Noble's new powers.<br><br><color orange>Be careful, {HeroName}. You fight under the looming shadow of Praetor Berry's tower. It will not be an easy fight by any means.</color> But your mission is perhaps the most important of all. Doing this will buy us enough time to gain allies from Primal Earth and to bring the fight to Cole. If you fall here, it means Cole will be able to muster his forces before Primal Earth can prepare itself. It will fall, and then too, shall the Resistance.<br><br><color Gold>Loyalists working undercover for Marchand should speak to him now regarding the activities of Dark Watcher.</color>"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3619833045" "Assault Neuron's Tower"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2115125954" "Good luck, {HeroName}. That is the best I can offer you at this moment in time."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P442461847" "<color deepskyblue>Finale: Paving the Future</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P2088767018" "Neuron's tower looms in front of you. Who knew that this would be the key to Cole's invasion of Primal Earth?"

